 "equipment_type": "Packaged rooftop unit controller (Series 100, 70-150 ton)",
 "applies_to": "YORK Series 100 YPAL single packaged rooftop units, 70-105 ton Mod F and 120-150 ton Mod G, with the IPU control board.",
 "summary": "The Series 100 rooftop's IPU control board speaks BACnet MS/TP on Port 1 and Modbus on Port 4. The table lists about 220 objects: analog inputs for air temperatures, pressures, airflows, CO2 and the unit mode; binary inputs for compressors, fans, heat stages and faults; analog values for setpoints, limits and BAS sensor inputs; and 0/1 BAS commands (occupancy, unit stop, morning warm-up, smoke purge, thermostat calls) published as both AVs and BVs.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": "23000 + MAC address",
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Access is from the READ/WRITE column. The table lists each 0/1 BAS command twice, as an AV (77-99) and a BV (1-23) with the same name; both are kept.",
  "Descriptions are the user interface names from the table. Points marked FlexSys, VAV, CV or a tonnage range only exist on those units.",
  "Units are taken from the description column where it states them (°F, \"WC, CFM, %, ppm, psig).",
  "The Modbus register addresses in the same table are not reproduced.",
  "The 70-105 ton Mod F IOM (100.50-NOM9, 8/2018) prints the same table; it marks AI 52 TEMP_2_SUPER as not available.",
  "The 50-65 ton Mod F list has extra fault, warning, hot gas reheat and BAS outdoor air objects and is a separate entry. The older ECO2 Mod D/E list (IPU 1) is also separate."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "Series 100 Single Packaged Rooftop Units 120-150 Ton, Mod G - Installation, Operation, Maintenance (Table 40, BACnet MS/TP, Modbus, BACnet IP)",
  "doc_number": "100.50-NOM11 (120)",
  "revision_date": "2020-01-20",
  "url": "https://docs.johnsoncontrols.com/ductedsystems/api/khub/documents/NM9Ffc7gf1w9ZMGJ4IEBhQ/content"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Connect to Port 1 of the IPU control board on BACnet MS/TP. Command occupancy with OCCUPNCY_CMD, stop or release the unit with UNIT_STOP and write the occupied zone setpoints; feed zone temperature through AV 40 if the control method is set to comm zone temp. Read supply air and zone temperatures, supply fan status, unit mode and the fault inputs.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "AV 88",
    "name": "OCCUPNCY_CMD",
    "why": "Occupancy command (1 = occupied)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 93",
    "name": "UNIT_STOP",
    "why": "Unit stop (1 = stopped, 0 = normal)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 21",
    "name": "OCC_ZN_COOL",
    "why": "Occupied zone cooling setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 22",
    "name": "OCC_ZN_HEAT",
    "why": "Occupied zone heating setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 58",
    "name": "UNIT_MODE",
    "why": "Current operating mode index"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 59",
    "name": "SUPPLY_FAN",
    "why": "Supply fan on/off"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 46",
    "name": "SUP_AIR_TEMP",
    "why": "Supply air temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 60",
    "name": "ZONE_TEMP",
    "why": "Zone temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 2",
    "name": "COL/HEAT_FLT",
    "why": "Cooling/heating fault (1 = faulted)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 54",
    "name": "SEN/MSC_FLT",
    "why": "Sensor/misc fault (1 = fault)"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "OCCUPNCY_CMD (AV 88 or BV 12) puts the unit in occupied (1) or unoccupied (0) mode and UNIT_STOP (AV 93 or BV 17) stops it (1) or returns it to normal operation (0). BAS reset and BAS sensor inputs must first be enabled at the unit with the SERVICE key; AV 40 zone temperature needs the control method set to comm zone temp.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": "AV 40 ZONE_TEMP_BAS feeds zone temperature when the control method is set to comm zone temp. AV 43 CO2_INSIDE and the BAS reset values (duct static, supply air) must be enabled with the SERVICE key before they are used.",
  "setup": [
   "Port 1 carries BACnet MS/TP (P1 PROTOCOL = BACNET); baud 1200 to 76800 is set with the SERVICE key.",
   "MAC address 0-127 from the IPU DIP switches or P1 MANUAL MAC ADDRESS; the device instance defaults to 23000 + MAC, or DE MODIFIER ADDRESS x 100 + DE MODIFIER OFFSET.",
   "Cycle main power after changing the MAC address or port settings.",
   "The Ethernet port is not functional; BACnet IP needs a gateway (the manual suggests a JCI NCE).",
   "LON and N2 need an E-Link gateway on Port 1."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Each 0/1 command is listed as both an AV and a BV with the same name; use one of them, not both.",
   "Points marked FlexSys, VAV, CV or 70-150 ton only report only on those units.",
   "Setpoint and status AIs report in imperial units."
  ]
 },
